#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""verify-test-efficacy — seeded behavioural defects must be caught by the product tests.

Each control copies the workspace to a temporary directory, injects ONE subtle defect into
production code, and runs the named test. The control passes only if that test FAILS as a test
(a compile error or a missing test is a broken control, not a detection). The canonical tree is
never edited; its digest is compared before and after.

Headless, deterministic, non-interactive. Exit status 0 only when every control detects its defect.
Usage: tools/verify-test-efficacy
"""

